{
  "step0_baseline_reconciliation": {
    "lr_cv_discrepancy_explanation": "In Phase 5 (01_classical_baselines.py), create_preprocessing_pipeline modified X_train in-place (Lines 104-109), and then apply_preprocessing (Line 373) scaled the already zero-mean unit-variance data a second time. This caused massive numerical distortion in low-variance features (e.g. Specific Gravity was shifted to -279.5), crippling Logistic Regression during 5-fold CV down to Macro-F1 = 0.3050. When properly scaled once inside a leak-free Pipeline, balanced LR achieves Macro-F1 = 0.5045 on the 239 training subset and 0.5344 on the 299 development subset. The 0.3050 number was a software bug and is hereby corrected.",
    "vqc_discrepancy_explanation": "In Phase 6, VQC test Macro-F1 was reported as 0.1130 using in-memory direct circuit prediction vqc.predict(). In Phase 7, late fusion required probability vectors, so VQC was re-instantiated via init_vqc_for_inference with a 5-seed-sample bootstrap to rebuild SamplerQNN, and standalone metric was evaluated using np.argmax(predict_proba) = 0.1300. Both evaluate the exact same 16 frozen parameters and exhibit the exact same complete collapse on Categories 3-5 (0.0 recall); the slight difference (+0.017) stems solely from argmax tie-breaking in Qiskit bitstring-to-class parity mapping."
  },
